Package: maluos-installer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.12), python3-yaml, casper, initramfs-tools, plymouth, plymouth-theme-spinner, maluos-branding (>= 0.4.0), mokutil, iproute2, squashfs-tools, python3-urwid, openssl, kbd, dosfstools, e2fsprogs, xfsprogs, lvm2, cryptsetup, efibootmgr, pciutils, curl, openssh-server
Description: MaluOS installer (the live medium's own)
 The installer the MaluOS medium boots into (Phase 11). maluos-install
 executes an install plan (docs/install-plan.md): guided layouts (direct or
 LVM, ext4 or xfs, LUKS optional), the image verified and unpacked, the
 target configured, the bootloader for BIOS and UEFI with Secure Boot, the
 first-boot file seeded, one telemetry report when the plan says so. A plan
 comes from maluos.plan= on the kernel command line (the medium's unattended
 plans, a URL, a labelled disk), from /maluos/plan/default.yaml, or over SSH
 (maluos.ssh=). A journal makes a failed install resumable. The package also
 carries the live configuration: casper.conf (the live user maluos), the
 console units, the on-media apt source. It is never installed on a target.